  "comment": "udev is the device manager for the Linux kernel . Primarily, it manages device nodes in /dev . It is the successor of devfs and hotplug, which means that it handles the /dev directory and all user space actions when adding/removing devices, including firmware load. Contents 1 History 2 Overview 3 Operation 4 Architecture 5 Authors 6 Referensi 7 Pranala Lain History udev was new in Linux 2.5. The",
